        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial forecast. The 45-day ceasefire extension was brokered in Washington talks and confirmed May 15 (Bloomberg, The National, CGTN). Both sides agreed to reconvene June 2–3. The May 6 Haret Hreik strike and May 13 highway strikes (Mount Lebanon governorate) show Israel willing to strike near Beirut but not inside the governorate post-May 6. Hezbollah disarmament remains unresolved. Base rate for ceasefire holding full 45 days, given ongoing violation rate, is moderate.</div>
