  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Iran's Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei made on-the-record statements on May 12 naming Iran's "14-point plan" by label — saying it "exclusively focuses on ending the war and contains no issues related to the nuclear domain" — carried by IranPress, Press TV, and CGTN sourced from Tasnim. President Pezeshkian's May 11 statement in CNBC/Reuters also addressed the diplomatic track by name. Both are named officials quoted in at least two qualifying outlets, meeting <span class="cite">F1</span>'s resolution criteria. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span></p>

      <p>Iran's negotiating team announced five preconditions for entering any second round of US talks — a full end to hostilities on all fronts, lifting of all sanctions, release of frozen assets, compensation for war damage, and recognition of Iran's rights over the Strait of Hormuz — reported by Fars News Agency and confirmed by CGTN (May 13) and USA News-Pravda (May 12). This is a pre-negotiation demand list, not a rejection. Baghaei described Iran's proposal as "reasonable and generous." No Kayhan editorial with explicit rejection language ("rad," "mardud") about the 14-point framework was found in the monitoring period. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>

      <p>Israel and Lebanon formally extended their ceasefire by 45 days in Washington talks on May 15, confirmed by Bloomberg, The National, and CGTN, with both sides agreeing to reconvene June 2–3. The IDF's May 13 drone strikes — which killed eight people including two children on the coastal highway near Jiyeh — landed approximately 20 kilometers south of Beirut in the Mount Lebanon governorate, not within Beirut governorate borders. Lebanese Health Ministry reporting (via Times of Israel and Al Jazeera, May 13) and geolocation place the strikes in the Jiyeh area; neither IDF nor the Lebanese government described them as Beirut strikes. The horizon for <span class="cite">F4</span> passed without a qualifying event. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Saudi Arabia and Kuwait lifted all restrictions on US military use of their bases and airspace on May 8 — confirmed by Reuters via Iran International, Middle East Monitor, WSJ (via Iran International), and multiple outlets on May 7-8 — following a second Trump-MBS phone call. <strong>JUDGE FLAG:</strong> <span class="cite">F5</span> resolution criteria requires BOTH KC-46 tanker tracks confirmed AND a Pentagon or Saudi MOFA press statement; Judge search found neither independently verified — Pentagon "referred questions to the White House" per NBC; Project Freedom did not restart after May 8 (Trump rejected Iran's proposal May 10-11). <span class="cite">F5</span> is flagged OPEN-AMBIGUOUS at p=0.85 pending human confirmation of KC-46 operational tracks or Pentagon statement text. Brent crude prices settled in the $105–$106 range on May 14-16 (CNBC, May 16 EIA data), reflecting partial diplomatic optimism, though Hormuz transits remained at roughly 5% of baseline per NBC/IranWarLive monitoring. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span> (open-ambiguous, human review), supports <span class="cite">F6</span> without move</p>

      <p>Netanyahu's coalition submitted a bill to dissolve the Knesset on May 13 (Washington Post, Times of Israel, JNS), signed by heads of all coalition factions including Shas, Degel HaTorah, and Likud, with the coalition retaining its 61-seat majority throughout. The dissolution push was triggered by the failure to pass ultra-Orthodox draft-exemption legislation. Sources quoted by Times of Israel placed the earliest preliminary vote at May 19-20. Araghchi arrived in New Delhi on May 13 for the BRICS Foreign Ministers' Meeting (ANI, Republic World), keeping multilateral diplomatic channels active outside the Pakistan-mediated bilateral track. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

