      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (30%):</strong> Iran's five-precondition demand blocks talks resumption (<span class="cite">F8</span> at 25%), Hormuz remains closed (<span class="cite">F6</span> at 30%), and renewed IDF action in the Beirut area triggers Hezbollah escalation (<span class="cite">F9</span> failure at 45%).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (45%):</strong> The 45-day Lebanon ceasefire holds (<span class="cite">F9</span>), Pakistan back-channels keep Iran-US contact alive at sub-envoy level, but the five-precondition gap prevents a signed memo (<span class="cite">F2</span> at 10%), and Hormuz stays effectively closed through June (<span class="cite">F6</span>).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (25%):</strong> Iran withdraws the Hormuz-sovereignty precondition under Chinese/Pakistani pressure, enabling a June negotiating session (<span class="cite">F8</span>), Brent retreats below $95, and the Lebanon ceasefire holds to June 29 (<span class="cite">F9</span>).</p>
